{
  "raw": {
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Academic-Coach_JREQ-001895-1": {
      "title": "Academic Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Academic coaches provide professional, student-centered coaching for individuals seeking a collaborative, consistent, and supportive partnership focused on academic growth and development. Through regular engagement, coaches empower students to develop academic self-awareness; build confidence, resilience, and perseverance; strengthen time management and organizational strategies; and improve communication skills with both peers and professionals. Coaches also guide students in identifying and utilizing appropriate resources to support their success. In addition to direct coaching, academic coaches are responsible for maintaining accurate records, achieving and maintaining certification as academic coaches, and participating in ongoing training and professional development. Key Outcomes 70% of time: Academic Coaching  Meet regularly with individual students to support academic growth, reinforce effective learning strategies, and model a professional mindset. Follow the Center’s academic coaching model, which emphasizes goal setting, reflective practices, and student empowerment. Demonstrate sensitivity to and understanding of diverse learning styles, intellectual development, executive functioning challenges, and psychosocial factors that may impact student success. 20% of time: Record Keeping and Communication Efficiently use the Center’s record management system to track student interactions and progress. Complete all required reports and participate in scheduled meetings with the Center Director to review student development. Maintain timely and clear communication with the Center Director regarding student progress and any concerns that arise. 10% of time: Certification and Professional Development Attend required training sessions to achieve and maintain the designation of “Professional Academic Coach” as established by the National Tutoring Association. Participate in mandatory professional development seminars. Engage in ongoing, optional development opportunities, such as mentoring partnerships and other Center-led initiatives to enhance coaching practices. Perform other duties as assigned Core Competencies Reliability able to get the job done, available, and engaged with the job and the Endicott community Organization organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time Communication Skills   has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing Adaptability shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently Follow Through  takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition Customer Service The employee anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner Initiative/Personal Leadership identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions Team Player   shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Master’s degree in a related field required; equivalent professional experience will be considered. Minimum of 2-3 years of experience in teaching, tutoring, academic coaching, counseling, or mentoring young adults preferred. Strong communication skills across written, verbal, and digital platforms required. Proficiency with, or willingness to learn, key technologies including Google Workspace, Microsoft Office, Canvas (LMS), email platforms, social media, internet research tools, and electronic scheduling/calendar systems.   Effective Date of Current Version:  June, 2025 In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $30.00–$40.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Dean--School-of-Nursing-and-Health-Sciences_JREQ-002613": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, School of Nursing and Health Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Associate Dean of Nursing Programs is a member of the leadership team for the School of Nursing. Under the direction of the Dean and in close collaboration with the Associate Dean of Undergraduate programs is responsible for leadership and oversight of the development, implementation, and evaluation of outstanding, innovative academic programs in the School of Nursing. This position assumes responsibility for the accreditation, curriculum development, and evaluation and assessment of all program outcomes .  The Associate Dean of Nursing Programs will provide leadership and direction to faculty and professional staff in the development of initiatives and academic activities that promote student success, help to meet expected program outcomes, as well as align with the Endicott College mission to provide students with meaningful experiential learning. An academic appointment, if applicable, will be determined separately in accordance with the College’s academic appointment process.   About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.  Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities  Lead the SON in successful program-level and institutional-level accreditation activities with all accreditation and oversight boards. (40%) Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE) Leads the SON in assessment and evaluation of all program outcomes. Develops, oversees, and implements the evaluation process of all programs, including survey development, refinement, and analysis of outcomes. Works with the Dean to develop and implement the systematic plan of evaluation and reporting to accreditation agencies. Ensure a high-quality graduate curriculum with exceptional program outcomes that features meaningful, innovative, and experiential teaching strategies in line with the mission of the School of Nursing and the college. (40%) Ensure licensure and certification success through oversight, implementation, and effective use of programs (Fitzgerald Course). Collaborate with Program Chairs regarding curricular needs for adjunct laboratory, simulation, and clinical faculty. Assist with the vetting, appointing, orienting, and mentoring of faculty members while also creating an atmosphere of inclusivity and community within the SON. Oversee regular performance evaluations of faculty and professional staff to ensure continuous improvement. Oversee direct reports and promote a positive and inclusive work environment that supports the professional growth of staff while fostering a commitment to academic innovation and excellence. Assist the Dean in development and management of the operating and capital budgets. Represent the SON in the community through participation in scholarship, service, and professional development activities that promote the school. (20%) Support Admission and Recruiting events – especially at the graduate level, which requires the Associate Dean to work very closely with the Admission/Recruiting and Marketing/Communications Department (website design) and program chairs to establish and implement effective recruiting measures for graduate programs. Attain revenue targets for the graduate programs. Advises students based on the needs of the school. Teaches 2 courses/year based on the needs of the school. Other duties as assigned Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community.  Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Doctorate in nursing or related field; experience with a professional accreditation; Effective verbal/written communication skills and proficiency in English language; Commitment to inclusive education and developing cultural competencies among faculty, staff, and students with a lens toward social justice; Documented record of academic scholarship in a related field; Demonstrated ability to mentor students at the undergraduate and graduate levels; Evidence of outstanding teaching competencies, including online, lab, and simulation; Evidence of a commitment to service; Active participation in professional organizations; Excellent interpersonal and collaborative skills with high interest in working with all levels of learners (traditional, non-traditional, and adult students); Self-directed with excellent organizational skills; Detail-oriented and student-centered are essential to the position; The position is based out of Beverly, MA; Strong computer experience, which must include the ability to work effectively with MS Office suite products, i.e., Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Google Suite (Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Forms), and Canvas Learning Management System. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026 In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $125,000-$165,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. To apply, please submit your resume/CV and a cover letter."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Dean--Undergrad-Nursing-Programs_JREQ-002612-1": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, Undergrad Nursing Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Associate Dean of Undergraduate Nursing Programs serves as a member of the School of Nursing leadership team. Reporting to the Dean and working in close collaboration with the Associate Dean of Nursing Programs and the Associate Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences, this position provides leadership and oversight for the development, implementation, and evaluation of innovative, high-quality undergraduate academic programs within the School of Nursing. The Associate Dean of Undergraduate Nursing Programs supports the advancement of academic excellence by guiding faculty and professional staff in the development of initiatives and academic activities that promote student success, support the achievement of expected program outcomes, and align with the Endicott College mission of providing meaningful experiential learning opportunities. An academic appointment, if applicable, will be determined separately in accordance with the College’s academic appointment process. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities Ensure a high-quality undergraduate curriculum with exceptional program outcomes, supported by meaningful, innovative, and experiential teaching strategies that align with the mission of the School of Nursing and the College. (25%) Monitor NCLEX pass rates at or above the School of Nursing’s expected level of achievement, while meeting accreditation benchmarks and state and national pass rate expectations. Support licensure success through the oversight, implementation, and effective use of student success and assessment resources, including ATI. Collaborate with undergraduate Program Chairs to identify curricular needs related to adjunct, laboratory, simulation, and clinical faculty. Assist with the vetting, appointment, orientation, and mentoring of faculty members while fostering a culture of inclusivity, collegiality, and community within the School of Nursing. Participate in hiring faculty for undergraduates and oversee their continued professional growth. Supervise direct reports and promote a positive, inclusive work environment that supports professional growth, academic innovation, and excellence. Assist the Dean with the development and management of operating and capital budgets. Ensure a positive and supportive student experience through direct oversight of student issues across all undergraduate nursing programs. (25%) Serve as the primary point of contact for undergraduate student issues in collaboration with Program Chairs, full-time faculty, academic advisors, and appropriate college departments, including Student Success, Housing, Health Services, Career Services, International Education, Community Service, the Chaplain’s Office, Athletics, the Registrar, Financial Aid, and Admissions. Provide leadership and support related to student progression, academic concerns, retention, professionalism, and overall student success across the undergraduate nursing programs. Collaborate with faculty, advisors, and college departments to address student needs in a timely, fair, consistent, and student-centered manner. Provide leadership and oversight for simulation centers and laboratories, clinical education, and internship experiences within the undergraduate nursing programs. (25%) Collaborate with the Director of Simulation and Labs and the Director of the Clinical Placement Office to ensure that: Experiential learning opportunities are meaningful, well-coordinated, and aligned with program outcomes. Clinical, simulation-based, and internship experiences strengthen students’ clinical judgment, professional development, and readiness for nursing practice. Faculty, clinical partners, and professional staff collaborate effectively to promote consistency, quality, and continuous improvement across experiential learning settings. Required accreditation processes, standards, and documentation are consistently followed, maintained, and evaluated in these areas Support School of Nursing operations, student advising, recruitment, and professional engagement through service to the school, college, and broader community. (15%) Support Admission and Recruiting events Advise students based on the needs of the school. Support the Academic Coordinator with the Course of Study and oversee student registration and scheduling concerns. Assist the SON in successful program-level and institutional-level accreditation activities with all accreditation and oversight boards. (10%) MA Board of Registration in Nursing (MABORN) Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE)  Other duties as assigned. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Doctorate in nursing or MSN with 5 years' experience in a related field; Effective verbal/written communication skills and proficiency in English language; Commitment to inclusive education and developing cultural competencies among faculty, staff, and students with a lens toward social justice; Documented record of academic scholarship in a related field; Demonstrated ability to mentor students at the undergraduate level; Evidence of outstanding teaching competencies, including online, lab, and simulation; Evidence of a commitment to service; Active participation in professional organizations; Excellent interpersonal and collaborative skills with high interest in working with all levels of learners (traditional, non-traditional, and adult students);  Self-directed with excellent organizational skills; Detail-oriented and student-centered are essential to the position; The position is based out of Beverly, MA;  Strong computer experience, which must include abilities to work effectively with MS Office suite products, i.e., Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Google Suite (Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Forms), and Canvas Learning Management System. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026 In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $125,000–$165,000 Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. To apply, please submit a resume/CV and cover letter."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Coach--Women-s-Track---Field-and-Men-s---Women-s-Cross-Country_JREQ-002461": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Track & Field and Men's & Women's Cross Country",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview Under the supervision of the Head Coach, the Assistant Coach of Women’s Track & Field, Men’s and Women’s Cross-Country programs will assist in all aspects of the cross-country and track and field programs as part of the Athletics Department.  These areas include, but are not limited to, recruiting, preparing training/practice plans, team travel arrangements, and competition planning and preparation.  The successful candidate will provide strong leadership and communication skills, demonstrate a philosophy that emphasize academic priorities for student-athletes, as well as a commitment to the growth of the Endicott community.  The Assistant Coach, Women’s Track & Field/Men’s & Women’s Cross-Country will ensure an understanding and adherence to NCAA Division III principles and Endicott College’s mission statement. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities Assist in organizing and administering all phases of the Cross Country/Track & Field Programs (50%) Commit to student-athlete growth and development towards academic success Assist in programming training, practice planning, and competition planning. Assist with all team operations and administrative duties. Assist with coordinating travel logistics including rentals and hotels. Retention of quality student-athletes Recruiting (40%) Communicate with prospective student-athletes via email, phone calls, and on-campus visits Attend high school competitions to meet with prospective student-athletes Maintain an organized recruiting system to ensure streamline communication between coaching staff and recruits Fulfill annual recruiting goals Community Engagement (5%) Assist Institutional Advancement in efforts to increase athletics revenue and alumni engagement (Giving Day, Golf Tournament, and other fundraising efforts). Cultivate relationships with alumni through fundraising efforts, alumni events, and outreach. Attend department meetings and be an active member of the Endicott Athletic Department. Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other Duties (5%) Other duties as assigned Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Coach, Women’s Track & Field/Men’s & Women’s Cross Country, and under general supervision of the Associate Director of Athletics and Director of Athletics. Supervisory Responsibilities None Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. 3 years coaching experience at the college level. Ability to work effectively with diverse groups and environments. Excellent verbal and written communication, interpersonal and public relations skills. Current adult CPR/AED certification. Strong organizational and problem-solving skills. Strong leadership skills. Ability to work as part of a team. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $36,000–$46,000 Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  June, 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Event-Operations--Coordinator_JREQ-002611": {
      "title": "Event Operations  Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Misselwood at Endicott College is a breathtaking oceanfront estate with historic charm, offering panoramic views and serving as the premier location for world-class events in Beverly, MA. We are seeking a vibrant and dynamic individual to join our Operations Team. Reporting to the Director of Events Operations, this role will support the efforts of the Operations Team, upholding Misselwood’s reputation for superior hospitality and seamless event execution. This is an exciting entry-level opportunity for a professional with exceptional organizational, customer service, and operational skills who excels in a dynamic environment and takes pride in delivering unforgettable experiences for clients and guests. The Event Operations Coordinator supports the planning, coordination, and execution of events with responsibility for small-scale events and operations tasks. This role assists the Misselwood Events department by managing logistics, handling administrative tasks, and ensuring effective communication between professional and seasonal teams. Nestled on the scenic coast, Misselwood Events is more than just a venue – it’s a destination where memories are made. As part of the Endicott College community, we offer a collaborative and professional environment that celebrates creativity and teamwork while delivering exceptional service.   Key Outcomes                                                                                                                     60% Logistics Coordination Coordinate and implement all details for Endicott-hosted programs, Misselwood events series, and small scale corporate day and overnight programs Perform administrative support tasks, including managing inbox correspondence, processing invoices, and maintaining operational records. Assist with scheduling seasonal staff Serve as a liaison between professional staff and seasonal team members to ensure clear communication and efficient event execution. Support Event Operation Managers will logistics and operational tasks 40% On-Site Operations Support the Operations Management team in ensuring the Misselwood House is ready to welcome guests and that day-to-day operations run smoothly. Assist with venue setup and teardown, ensuring all materials, signage, equipment, and supplies are in place before, during, and after events. Maintain inventory, submit maintenance requests, and support operational needs Perform other duties as assigned to contribute to the successful execution of events and daily operations. Core Competencies Reliability able to get the job done, available, and engaged with the job and the Endicott community Organization organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time Communication Skills has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing Adaptability shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently Follow Through takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition Customer Service customer-focused with a passion for delivering exceptional service. Employee anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner Initiative/Personal Leadership identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions Team Player shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members   Knowledge/Skills/Abilities                                                                                                                     Bachelor’s degree in event management, hospitality, or a related field is required. 1-2 years of experience in event coordination, customer service, or related field is preferred. Availability to work evenings, weekends, and flexible hours as needed. Physical ability to lift up to 40 pounds and remain on your feet for extended periods. Proven ability to manage multiple events simultaneously in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Exceptional customer service skills with a proactive, solution-oriented approach. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with keen attention to detail and accuracy. Outstanding organizational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritize tasks and remain composed under pressure. Proficiency in Google Workspace and adaptability to new platforms. Ability to take initiative, think proactively, and maintain professionalism during stressful situations. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Commitment to timely and respectful communication, including responding to emails and voicemails. ServeSafe, Crowd Manager, and AED/CPR certifications (or willingness to obtain). In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $50,000–$60,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Coach--Women-s-Lacrosse_JREQ-002608-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Women’s Lacrosse Assistant Coach in the Department of Athletics, reporting to the Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach, is responsible for working in conjunction with the Head Coach in all facets required for an NCAA Division III Women’s Lacrosse program, including an understanding and adherence to NCAA Division III principles and Endicott College’s mission statement. This position is a 10 month annual work period, is expected to be on-site with some travel, and is 35 hours per week. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities 60%--- Talent Identification, Recruiting & Admissions Engagement  ● Identify and recruit talented, academically qualified prospective student-athletes who align with Division III standards and program values.  ● Maintain direct, professional communication with prospects, families, and high school/club coaches.  ● Represent the program at major regional and national recruiting tournaments across the fall, winter, and summer.  ● Manage prospect evaluations, phone logs, emails, and contact records accurately within Teamworks.  ● Partner closely with the Office of Admission to recruit an incoming class commensurate for the institution and program.  ● Conduct early academic reads, targeting a 50%+ conversion rate from early reads to early commitments.  ● Attend the annual IWLCA Convention for professional development and engage with the sport’s national governing body.  30% — Program Administration, On-Field Development & Operations ● Assist the Head Coach in planning and executing daily practices, game strategy, opponent scouting, and in-season film breakdown.  ● Streamline day-to-day administrative operations using Workday and departmental software.  ● Support athlete retention, holistic growth, academic progress, and the seamless transition of transfer student-athletes.  ● Assist with program fundraising initiatives, clinic operations, alumni relations, and public relations efforts.  10% — Game Day Operations & Departmental Support  Lead assigned game-day event management duties, including facility setup/breakdown, crowd control, and student worker supervision. Perform additional administrative tasks and special projects as assigned by the Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach and Athletic Director.  Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other duties as assigned Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Coach, W. Lacrosse. Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills • Bachelor's Degree • 3-5 years successful experience coaching and recruiting women’s lacrosse at the high school and/or college level.  • The ability to work effectively with diverse groups and environments. • Effective communication, interpersonal and public relations skills. • Current adult CPR/AED certification;  • Strong written, oral and organizational and problem-solving skills • Working knowledge of computer software applications  • Strong leadership skills  Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred.  TeamWorks IWLCA Sports Recruits Hudl Google Sheets/Docs/Drive Effective Date of Current Version:  August 2026 In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $36,000–$40,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Director--Operations---Systems--Internship---Career-Center_JREQ-002578": {
      "title": "Director, Operations & Systems, Internship & Career Center",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Director of Internship Operations & Systems , reporting to the Dean, Internship & Career Center, provides strategic and operational leadership for the systems, processes, technology, data, and assessment infrastructure that support the Internship & Career Center's experiential learning and career initiatives. The Director is responsible for the effective design, implementation, oversight, and continuous improvement of department-wide internship operations and technology systems. This position serves as the Center's primary leader for technology and operational systems, ensuring that processes are efficient, data is accurate and accessible, systems are effectively utilized, and stakeholders receive appropriate training and support. The Director works collaboratively with students, faculty, academic leadership, staff, employer partners, internship sites, and institutional offices including Information Technology, the Research Center, and Communications & Marketing. The position leads cross-functional initiatives, develops and maintains operational standards and procedures, analyzes data and outcomes, and makes recommendations to departmental leadership regarding technology, processes, reporting, and continuous improvement. Through effective operational leadership and data-informed decision-making, the Director helps ensure consistent and high-quality internship processes, meaningful assessment of career and experiential learning outcomes, effective use of technology, and clear communication of Endicott's experiential learning model and student success. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities Leadership and oversight of Internship & Career Center technology and systems (40%) Provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for technology systems supporting the Internship & Career Center, including Symplicity/Gulls@Work, Workday, related databases, reporting tools, and other systems used to support internship and experiential learning operations. Serves as the primary departmental liaison with Information Technology, external technology vendors, and other institutional partners regarding system implementation, integration, functionality, data management, and ongoing system support. Leads the implementation, enhancement, and continuous improvement of technology systems and workflows to support the Center's operational and strategic priorities. Oversees the seamless transfer and integration of data between Symplicity/Gulls@Work and Workday, including initial configuration, ongoing data transfers, integrations, and system buildouts. Establishes and maintains standards and processes that promote data accuracy, integrity, security, accessibility, and timely reporting. Leads the development and delivery of technology training for students, faculty, staff, employer partners, and internship host sites. Develops training materials, user guides, FAQs, and other resources to support effective system adoption. Monitors system functionality, identifies opportunities for improvement, and coordinates the resolution of system issues with internal IT staff and external vendors. Evaluates emerging technologies and best practices in career services, experiential education, and higher education operations and makes recommendations regarding technology selection, implementation, renewal, and purchasing. Develops and oversees recurring and ad hoc Workday and Symplicity/Gulls@Work reporting for the Provost, Deans, faculty, and other institutional stakeholders. Maintains required system configurations, credentials, integrations, and API access to ensure reliable registration, data collection, and reporting capabilities. Advises departmental leadership on technology strategy, system capabilities, operational risks, and opportunities to improve efficiency and stakeholder experience. Leads internship operations, processes, and continuous improvement (40%) Provides leadership and oversight for department-wide internship processes, procedures, policies, timelines, and operational standards. Develops, documents, implements, and continuously improves internship processes to promote consistency, efficiency, accountability, and a high-quality experience for students, faculty, academic leaders, and internship partners. Establishes and maintains standards for internship evaluations, data collection, documentation, and data synthesis in collaboration with relevant stakeholders. Communicates key internship dates, requirements, processes, and timelines to Internship Faculty, Academic Deans, and other stakeholders and monitors student progress toward completion. Coordinates cross-functional processes with Information Technology, the Research Center, Communications & Marketing, academic departments, and other institutional partners related to internship proposals, graduate surveys, employer evaluations, student outcomes, and reporting. Serves as a central operational resource for Internship Faculty and Academic Deans, providing guidance on processes, systems, data, timelines, and related operational matters. Identifies operational challenges and opportunities and develops recommendations to improve processes, technology utilization, communication, and stakeholder experience. Oversees the accuracy and effectiveness of information related to Internship & Career Center processes, policies, and resources across the Endicott website, internship database and search engine, Gulls@Work end-user FAQ site, and Internship & Career Center Hub. Leads coordination with Communications & Marketing to identify internship sites, students, and outcomes appropriate for website content, marketing features, and institutional communications. Collaborates with the Research Center to analyze supervisor evaluation data and identify trends, gaps, and opportunities that can inform departments, schools, and academic leadership. Collaborates with Communications & Marketing to translate internship and career outcomes data into reports, graphics, and other materials that communicate the impact of Endicott's experiential learning model. Leads or contributes to cross-functional projects and process-improvement initiatives that advance the strategic priorities of the Internship & Career Center. Leads operational assessment, data analysis, and outcomes reporting (20%) Provides operational leadership for assessment initiatives that evaluate the effectiveness, reach, and outcomes of Internship & Career Center programs and services. Collaborates with the Director of Assessment and departmental leadership to establish assessment processes, goals, measures, and reporting practices aligned with departmental and institutional priorities. Leads the administration, data collection, analysis, and reporting associated with the annual career outcomes survey for internal and external stakeholders. Uses reporting capabilities within department technology systems to analyze participation, engagement, and utilization data, including demographic information, to evaluate outreach and marketing efforts and identify opportunities to increase engagement among underrepresented student populations. Develops reports and data summaries that provide actionable insights to departmental and academic leadership. Identifies trends and opportunities in internship participation, career outcomes, technology utilization, and student engagement and makes recommendations for process or program improvements. Maintains appropriate documentation and reporting practices to support institutional assessment, strategic planning, accreditation, and other internal or external reporting needs. Other duties as assigned. Leadership and Collaboration Serves as a departmental leader and subject matter expert in internship operations, technology systems, data management, reporting, and operational assessment. Builds effective working relationships across academic and administrative units and represents the Internship & Career Center in relevant institutional initiatives and projects. Leads meetings, projects, training initiatives, and cross-functional working groups as assigned. Communicates complex operational, technological, and data-related information clearly to technical and non-technical audiences. Provides guidance and recommendations to the Dean and other departmental and academic leaders regarding operational priorities, systems, processes, and continuous improvement. Promotes a culture of continuous improvement, collaboration, accountability, and data-informed decision-making. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree preferred. Five or more years of progressively responsible professional experience in operations, technology systems, career services, experiential education, higher education administration, assessment, data management, or a related field. Demonstrated experience leading complex operational processes, projects, or cross-functional initiatives. Demonstrated experience managing or providing functional leadership for technology systems, databases, integrations, or enterprise applications. Experience analyzing data and developing reports, dashboards, or other materials that support organizational decision-making. Demonstrated ability to develop, implement, document, and improve policies, procedures, workflows, and operational standards. Experience working collaboratively with multiple internal and external stakeholders, including academic leaders, faculty, staff, technology partners, and vendors. Strong analytical, organizational, project management, and problem-solving skills. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with technical and non-technical audiences. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and work effectively in a complex, collaborative environment. Familiarity with technology and systems used in career services, experiential education, internship management, or higher education preferred. Experience with Symplicity/Gulls@Work, Workday, survey platforms, data reporting tools, or comparable systems preferred. Commitment to supporting student success, experiential learning, career development, and inclusive access to institutional resources. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $ 85,000.00- $ 95,000.00 . Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  August 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor--Interior-Architecture_JREQ-002579": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Interior Architecture",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Assistant Professor of Interior Architecture, in the Architectural Design Studies Department, reporting to the Associate Dean/Chair of Architectural Design Studies, teaches courses for the School of Visual and Performing Arts. They also advise students, participate in accreditation processes, engage in professional scholarship or development, assist in developing internship relationships and student opportunities, and participate in school- and college-wide service. They will teach courses and advise students for two semesters per academic year. This position is covered by the Collective Bargaining Agreement between the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA) and Endicott College. ECFA is a faculty union organized under the NEA (National Education Association) and provides structure and support for all full-time faculty at Endicott College. This is a 9-month position. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities The Assistant Professor of Interior Architecture teaches a variety of studio and lecture courses in the Architectural Studies and Interior Architecture programs at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful candidate will advise students, contribute to curriculum development and accreditation efforts, engage in professional scholarship and creative activity, foster internship partnerships and experiential learning opportunities, and participate actively in service to the School, College, and profession. Candidates should be comfortable teaching both traditional hand-drawing and physical model-making alongside advanced digital design and visualization tools and demonstrate a commitment to preparing students for an evolving, technology-driven design profession. Teach 24 credits per academic year (12 credits each semester) at the undergraduate and/or graduate level, typically equivalent to four lecture courses per semester. Advise up to 25 undergraduate and graduate students. Maintain regular office hours and provide academic mentoring and support to students. Participate in curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation activities. Engage in professional development, scholarship, creative activity, research, and/or publication. Attend and actively participate in department, school, and college meetings. Contribute to service at the department, school, college, and professional levels. Participate in undergraduate and graduate recruitment efforts, including evening and weekend Admission events. Perform other duties as assigned and in accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement between the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA) and Endicott College. Qualifications and Skills Terminal degree in Interior Architecture or a closely related discipline NCIDQ certification or the ability to obtain certification within two years of employment. Ability to teach a range of undergraduate and graduate courses in Interior Architecture, with expertise in sustainable design and other areas of contemporary interior architecture practice. Proficiency with industry-standard software, including Adobe Creative Suite, Revit, SketchUp, and AutoCAD. Demonstrate expertise in the complete interior architecture design process, incorporating building systems and codes, and be skilled in sketching and model making. Interest in incorporating emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence (AI), into design education and professional practice. Familiarity with the standards and accreditation processes of the Council for Interior Design Accreditation (CIDA) and the National Association of Schools of Art and Design (NASAD). Two to four years of college-level teaching experience preferred.  Three to five years of professional experience in interior architecture or interior design   (knowledge or experience in healthcare design is a plus) Strong interpersonal, collaborative, and communication skills with the ability to work effectively as part of a team. Demonstrated commitment to student-centered teaching, mentorship, and experiential learning in a teaching-focused institution. Effective Date of Current Version:  August 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Per-Diem-Athletic-Trainers_JREQ-002298": {
      "title": "Per Diem Athletic Trainers",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Per Diem Athletic Trainer in the Athletic Department, reporting to the Head Athletic Trainer, is responsible for providing temporary, on-site coverage for athletics events (in-season practices and contests, non-traditional contests, post-season contests, camps and skills clinics) for all varsity or club teams at the discretion of the Head Athletic Trainer. Duties can include care and prevention of athletic injuries, wellness promotion, examination, assessment, diagnosis, immediate care, emergency care, therapeutic intervention, healthcare organization, administration and professional responsibility for all varsity and club student-athletes and on-site practice/contest coverage. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.  Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities  Provide Athletic Training Services (70%)  o Provide on-site athletic training services for practices and athletic contests hosted by Endicott College.  o Comply with all NCAA, Conference affiliated, athletic department, industry, and institutional guidelines, recommendations, and regulations.  o The employee will be a person of integrity with high ethical standards that adheres to the NATA Code of Ethics and institutional guidelines. Adheres to the state practice act, all NATA and NCAA best practices, and standing orders specified by the team physician.  o Provides counseling and education of student-athletes within the scope of practice.  Evaluate Athletic Injuries and Illnesses (20%)  o Evaluate athletic injuries and illness sustained by a varsity or club student-athlete and refer to other health care professionals as necessary.  o Provide urgent and emergent care as needed by the situation following NATA and NCAA best practices.  o Provide treatment and rehabilitation exercises for athletic injuries or illnesses as needed    Administrative Duties (10%)  o Document all injuries and treatments provided and communicate injuries with full time Athletic Training staff  o Maintain cleanliness and safety of the equipment in the Athletic Training clinic(s)  o Works with the coaching staff and other Athletic Department personnel to ensure the safety of all facilities, environments, and equipment used for intercollegiate athletics  Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Athletic Trainer Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community.  Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills   ● Minimum of a Bachelor’s degree in Athletic Training  ● Valid national certification from the BOC  ● Valid CPR/AED Certification  ● Valid Massachusetts State licensure through the Board of Allied Health Professionals  ● Demonstrated ability to interact effectively with college-age students  ● Strong verbal and written communication skills  ● Possesses the ability to lift heavy objects, stand for long periods, work in various environmental conditions  ● Assist injured individuals on/off playing surfaces  ● Coverage can include availability of mornings, evenings, weekends, and holidays  ● Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters    Preferred Qualifications N/A  In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $53.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version: December 2025"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Banquet-Server_JREQ-002549": {
      "title": "Banquet Server",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview   The Wylie Inn and Conference Center is seeking Full Time Banquet Servers to join their team of dedicated professionals The Wylie Inn & Conference Center employees are part of the Endicott College community and share in the beautiful campus offerings. Endicott is located 20 miles north of Boston and accessible by public transportation. The parking is free and the beautiful beaches are close by! Situated on a picturesque stretch of the Atlantic Coast on Boston’s North Shore, the Wylie Inn and Conference Center at Endicott College offers well appointed, comfortable accommodations with an on-site café restaurant and bar; state of the art IACC certified conference center and an elegant social event venue, upper Manor. The Wylie Inn and Conference Center is ideal for a weekend getaway, retreat or conference. This lush 10-acre inn and conference center is just minutes away from historic downtown Salem, restaurants, scenic Cape Ann, shopping, museums and more.   About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   Key Responsibilities   ·        Set up banquet room as instructed by Banquet Captain to include linen, service ware and glassware ·        Attend roll call meetings before events to learn function particulars, including guest and hotel expectations ·        Greet guests and respond to requests in a friendly and courteous manner ·        Serve the food and/or beverage in the order and to the expectation of the Banquet Captain to ensure consistency in the order throughout the banquet ·        Promptly bus dishes as guests complete each course and/or meal at the end of the meal or function   Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible.   Other Duties   ·        Other duties as assigned   Reporting St ructure Reports to the Food Director with Direct Supervision   Supervisory Responsibilities   No supervisory responsibilities.   Core Competencies   Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills   ·        Minimum 18 years old ·        Ability to work in a standing position for long period of time ·        Ability to lift up to 25 pounds, maneuvering trays of food and drink ·        Ability to work well under pressure in a high-volume event ·        Positive attitude In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $18.00-20.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version:  February 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Technical-Assistant--Performing-Arts_JREQ-002566": {
      "title": "Technical Assistant, Performing Arts",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Technical Assistant in the Center for the Arts and Department of Performing Arts, reporting to the Audio Arts Technician, provides technical support for theatrical productions, concerts, rehearsals, and special events across campus. The position is responsible for assisting with the preparation, operation, and strike of productions, ensuring that performances and events are executed safely, efficiently, and professionally. This position supports periods of high production activity throughout the academic year, particularly during production weeks and at the end of each semester. Work is performed primarily during evenings and weekends, with a flexible schedule based on departmental production needs. This is a part-time position, working up to 19 hours per week, and is not eligible for benefits. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. Key Responsibilities Production Setup, Operation, and Strike (45%) Assist with the setup, operation, and breakdown of theatrical productions, concerts, rehearsals, and special events. Set up and strike production equipment, including amplifiers, microphones, speakers, lighting instruments, musical instruments, and related audio equipment. Assemble and dismantle staging elements, including risers, scenic walls, masking legs, curtains, backdrops, and other theatrical equipment. Assist with scene changes and backstage operations during performances. Support productions in the Rose Theater, Tia's Black Box Theater, and other campus venues. Lighting and Audio Support (30%) Hang, focus, move, and maintain theatrical lighting instruments and associated cabling. Assist with theatrical electrical work, including running power and signal cables while following established safety procedures. Assist with audio system installation, wiring, troubleshooting, and strike. Support programming and operation of theatrical lighting control systems and lighting cues. Support programming and operation of digital sound consoles, playback systems, and sound cues. Scenic Construction and Technical Maintenance (15%) Assist with scenic construction, light carpentry, painting, and maintenance of scenery and production equipment. Help maintain technical spaces, including organization of scenery, lumber, tools, hardware, cables, and storage areas. Assist with inventory management and maintenance of technical equipment and supplies. Technology Support (10%) Support projection systems, video playback, computer-based production technologies, AI-assisted production tools, and other emerging technical systems as appropriate. Perform other technical duties in support of productions and special events. Other duties as assigned. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Reporting Structure Reports to the Audio Arts Technician. Works under general supervision while exercising sound judgment and initiative in completing assigned production and technical support responsibilities. Supervisory Responsibilities May provide day-to-day direction, training, and oversight to student employees. While student employees formally report to the Audio Arts Technician, the Technical Assistant may serve as the designated lead or proxy during assigned shifts or projects. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills High school diploma or equivalent required. Minimum of 2 years of experience in theatrical production, live events, stagecraft, or a related field. Experience in one or more areas of theatrical production, including lighting, audio, scenery, stagecraft, or live event production. Basic carpentry skills and familiarity with hand and power tools. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced production environment. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to adapt to changing production schedules and priorities. Availability to work evenings and weekends based on the production calendar. Ability to safely lift, carry, push, and move up to 50 pounds. Ability to climb ladders, work safely at heights, and safely operate hand and power tools and other production equipment. Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters. Preferred Qualifications Working knowledge of theatrical lighting systems, sound reinforcement systems, and digital control consoles. Experience with theatrical electrical systems and rigging practices. Experience with projection systems, video playback, and computer-based production technologies. Experience working in an educational, community, or professional performing arts venue. Familiarity with emerging production technologies, including AI-assisted production tools. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $25.000–$30.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  July, 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Residence-Life-Operations-Coordinator_JREQ-002540": {
      "title": "Residence Life Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Job Summary This position combines responsibilities in Residence Life/ Campus Center Operations and Misselwood Events.  During the academic year, Residence Life Operations Coordinator (RLOC) reports to the Associate Director and manages off-campus leased housing and residential operations and also supports campus programming. During the summer months, the RLOC reports to the Executive Director, Misselwood Events and partners with the Operations staff to manage external overnight programs. This includes training and supervising student staff and coordinating event logistics. This is a full-time, 12-month, live-in position. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Outcomes 60% Residential Community, Student Center Operations, & Summer Event Management Foster a safe, inclusive, and developmentally supportive residential community by managing occupancy processes (check-ins/outs, room changes, roommate agreements, and health and safety inspections). Cultivate collaborative partnerships with leasing offices and campus stakeholders to enhance the student experience in college-leased housing. Contribute to departmental operations, including housing selection and break closings, ensuring effective and student-centered service delivery. Recruit, train, supervise, and evaluate student staff (Student Engagement Ambassadors and Late Night LoCa), promoting leadership development, accountability, and inclusive practices. Design, implement, and assess late-night and campus programming (~24 programs/semester), applying student development theory and assessment practices to enhance engagement and learning outcomes. Oversee weekly campus traditions (e.g., Tuesday Night Trivia), fostering community building and student involvement through collaborative partnerships. Advise and support Involvement Assistants in program planning, promotion, and execution, encouraging student leadership and co-curricular learning. Collaborate with Campus Center staff to support event operations, scheduling, and assessment, contributing to a welcoming and inclusive campus environment. Supervise summer student staff and coordinate conference/overnight programs, emphasizing customer service, operational excellence, and student staff development. Serve as a liaison between student staff and Event Operations leadership to ensure effective communication and seamless program implementation. Oversee summer residential operations (e.g., linens, facility readiness, prepping access cards, meal cards, physical keys, and housing sheets), ensuring quality service and operational efficiency. 20%: Student Support, Conduct, & On-Call Participate in the professional on-call rotation, responding to student crises and emergencies using sound judgment, ethical decision-making, and institutional protocols. Serve as a student conduct hearing officer, facilitating educational and restorative approaches to accountability in alignment with community standards. Support student well-being and success by addressing concerns with empathy, cultural competence, and appropriate referrals. Provide on-call support for summer residential communities as needed. 20%: Departmental Initiatives, Assessment, & Continuous Improvement Advance the residential curriculum and student engagement efforts through intentional programming and collaborative initiatives. Utilize assessment strategies to evaluate program effectiveness and inform continuous improvement. Research and implement best practices in student engagement, residential education, and summer/overnight programming. Develop and refine operational processes related to summer housing, group coordination, and resource management. Participate in departmental planning, training, and summer resource meetings to support strategic goals and organizational effectiveness. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other Duties Other duties as assigned Reporting Structure Reports to the Associate Director, Residence Life during the academic year and then reports to the Executive Director, Misselwood Events during the summer months. Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities Supervises student workers Core Competencies Reliability able to get the job done, available, and engaged with the job and the Endicott community Organization organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time Communication Skills   has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing Adaptability shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently Follow Through takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition Customer Service The employee anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner Initiative/Personal Leadership identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions Team Player shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Demonstrated ability to build positive relationships with students, colleagues, and external partners. Strong verbal and written communication skills across diverse audiences. Proven ability to supervise, train, and mentor student staff. Effective conflict resolution and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and adapt in a fast-paced, hybrid work environment. Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion, with the ability to work effectively with individuals from varied backgrounds. Strong customer service orientation and ability to respond to student and client needs with professionalism and care. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain composure in high-pressure or emergency situations. Access to a car needed to conduct “rounds” and to go off campus in emergencies, if needed Ability to work a flexible schedule, nights and weekends included. Preferred Qualifications Experience collaborating across departments and managing campus or external partnerships. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, particularly in managing student-facing processes. Experience with event planning, coordination, or campus programming. Ability to balance administrative responsibilities with student engagement and support In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $45,000- 47,000 and housing is included. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cummings-Center-for-Nursing-and-Health-Sciences/Assistant-Professor--Doctor-of-Nursing-Practice--DNP-_JREQ-002184-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing teaches courses for the Graduate Nursing Program. They also advise students, participate in accreditation processes; engage in professional scholarship or development, assist in the development of internship relationships and student opportunities, and participate in school and college-wide service. They will teach courses and advise students for two semesters.   This position is covered by the Collective Bargaining Agreement between the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA) and Endicott College. ECFA is a faculty union organized under the NEA (National Education Association) and provides structure and support for all full-time faculty at Endicott College.  The Cummings School of Nursing and Health Sciences is seeking a dynamic, full-time DNP Faculty member passionate about shaping the next generation of healthcare executives and clinical experts. As a vital educator in our growing Doctor of Nursing Practice program, you will leverage your expertise in healthcare leadership and clinical inquiry to teach advanced courses in both quantitative and qualitative methodologies. If you are ready to inspire doctoral students and drive innovation in healthcare delivery, this is your opportunity to make a lasting institutional impact. In this pivotal role, you will directly influence patient outcomes by championing Evidence-Based Practice (EBP) and Quality Improvement (QI) initiatives within our curriculum. You will have the opportunity to mentor, advise, and guide students through their culminating DNP Scholarly Practice Projects, translating evidence based practice into real-world clinical solutions. If you hold a Doctor of Nursing Practice degree, possess a strong background in organizational leadership, and thrive in a collaborative academic environment, apply today to join our forward-thinking nursing faculty. This is a year round position. Responsibilities include:  Teach 24 credits per academic year -- 12 credits in both the fall and spring semesters (4 lecture courses each semester, or equivalent). Advise up to 25 students.  Attend department, school, and college meetings.  Participate in accreditation processes.  Engage in professional development, scholarship, research, and/or publishing.  Assist in curriculum development.   Participate in department, school, and college service.  Maintain and post regular office hours.   Perform other duties as required and as outlined in the Collective Bargaining Agreement between the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA) and Endicott College.  Participate in course development and implementation.  Evaluate teaching/learning activities  Participate in governance, including the School of Nursing All School Committee and other committees as appointed   Requirement / Qualifications A doctorate in Nursing or a related field is required Must have or be eligible for RN licensure in Massachusetts Hold at least one graduate degree in nursing in the area of specialization required for the faculty appointment 3-5 years of experience in the related field of nursing Prior teaching experience in a nursing program is desired, and required at the Associate Professor Level Demonstrated ability to relate to a diverse student body Commitment to scholarship appropriate to the rank Demonstrate excellent interpersonal and collaborative skills In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the compensation for this faculty position is established through the College’s contractual salary structure. Pay rates are set for each faculty rank and appointment type. This position carries a fixed annual salary of $98,602.12 (Assistant Professor) or $115,161.61 (Associate Professor) for a 12-month appointment. This amount represents base salary only and does not include benefits or other forms of compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Director--Criminal-Justice-Graduate-Program_JREQ-002538": {
      "title": "Director, Criminal Justice Graduate Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Director of the Criminal Justice (CJ) Graduate Program in the School of Social Sciences, Communication, & Humanities reports to the Associate Dean. The Director is responsible for leading the strategic launch, growth, and daily operations of a newly designed CJ Graduate Program, which features a soft launch in Spring 2027 and full implementation in Fall 2027. This role includes managing curriculum development, supervising full and part-time faculty, overseeing program evaluation/accreditation, and driving student enrollment and retention. This is an in-person, on-campus position. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities Dedicated to Student Success (30%) Directs graduate academic advising, guiding students from admission through progression and successful completion of their degree. Implements a proactive advising model, including onboarding new advisees prior to program entry and conducting regular progress checks. Collaborates with the Associate Dean to identify, support, and coach at-risk students to maximize retention. Maintains high-quality advising standards to ensure timely student progress through coursework and career alignment. Contributes to the overall success of the CJ graduate program (30%) Leads the successful implementation and execution of the new CJ graduate program’s soft launch (Spring 2027) and full launch (Fall 2027) in coordination with the Associate Dean. Partners closely with the Homeland Security Graduate Program Director to integrate existing HLS concentration courses into the CJ curriculum and provide seamless cross-program pathways for students. Collaborates with the Director of the Cybercrime Forensics Lab to coordinate the cybersecurity concentration, including lab exercises, simulations, and hands-on training. Drives recruitment, enrollment growth, and student retention initiatives to sustain an 80%+ retention and graduation rate. Manages ongoing program assessment, continuous improvement, and accreditation efforts at the course, program, and school levels. Contributes to the College community through service on school-wide and institutional committees. Teaches and develops courses in CJ/HLS graduate programs (20%) Teaches 2 graduate-level courses per year across the CJ and HLS programs. Demonstrates excellence in teaching through strong student evaluations and the utilization of diverse, effective assessment strategies. Develops cutting-edge course content and materials aligned with current industry trends, program needs, and School standards. Supervises, trains, and evaluates adjunct faculty (10%) Collaborates with the Associate Dean to recruit, hire, train, and evaluate part-time adjunct faculty within the CJ graduate program. Ensures all adjunct faculty align their courses with Canvas LMS standards and School pedagogical benchmarks. Reviews student course evaluations annually with faculty to implement data-driven pedagogical adjustments. Increases Endicott’s reputation in the field of CJ graduate education (10%) Maintains an active track record of scholarship and research in criminal justice or a related field. Represents the College and its graduate programs through the presentation of academic scholarship at national and state conferences, seminars, or through peer-reviewed publications. Other duties as assigned. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Reporting Structure The Director of the Criminal Justice Graduate Program in the School of Social Sciences, Communication, & Humanities reports to the Associate Dean. Supervisory Responsibilities Collaborates with the Associate Dean to hire, supervise, train, and evaluate 100% of part-time graduate adjunct professors. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Ph.D. or terminal degree in Criminal Justice, Criminology, or a closely related field highly preferred ; a Master’s degree or JD with significant academic leadership and operational experience considered. Documented record of academic scholarship and active participation in national or regional professional organizations. Demonstrated excellence in graduate-level teaching, including experience with online, lab-based, or hybrid simulation models. Strong collaborative skills with a proven ability to work across departments (e.g., working alongside Homeland Security or Cybersecurity disciplines). Commitment to inclusive education, social justice, and developing cultural competencies among a diverse, non-traditional, and adult student population. Excellent organizational and technical proficiency, including experience with Canvas LMS, MS Office, and Google Workspace. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $94,000 .00   and $115,000.00. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  July 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--School-of-Nursing-Undergraduate_JREQ-002457": {
      "title": "Adjunct, School of Nursing Undergraduate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-25\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The Undergraduate Program in the School of Nursing is currently seeking individuals to teach courses in the Fall 2026 semester. All courses meet in accordance with the course delivery model discussed with your Director or the Dean. Adjunct faculty are expected to: Deliver the course(s) as discussed with the Director or Dean in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the Dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Bachelor’s degree with five years RN experience or enrolled in a Master’s degree is required for clinical faculty.  A minimum of a Master’s degree is required for didactic courses, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Coach--Roller-Hockey--Seasonal-_JREQ-002134-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Roller Hockey (Seasonal)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Assistant Roller Hockey Coach in the Athletic Department, reporting to the Associate Director of Athletics collaborates with the athletics department advisor and team leaders to set goals, develop budgets, evaluate organizational needs, problem-solve, and serve as a liaison with other college departments essential to program implementation and success.This is a part-time, seasonal position and is a fantastic opportunity to work with a thriving collegiate club to play a key role in the clubs continued development and success. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities The Assistant Coach will be inheriting a group of highly talented and motivated men that have continued to compete at Nationals every year. Coaching Duties (80%) Providing instruction, mentoring and guidance to student athletes to allow them to develop their athletic skills and abilities to maximum potential. Evaluating athletic ability and performance. Assuring that equipment and practice plans are prepared in advance of practice sessions. Maintaining positive and professional relations with students, athletes, and alumni Ability to teach safe and proper technique to beginning level players while challenging and integrating the skills of higher-level players Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other duties as assigned Program Administrative Support (20%) Coordinate scheduling, meals, transportation, etc for all team trips in conjunction with the head coach Track team expenses and process invoices Please note: Under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), position descriptions should focus on essential functions , those that, if removed, would fundamentally change the job. Reporting Structure Reports to the Associate Director, Athletics. Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities None Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Minimum education or training needed to be considered for the role At least one year of relevant experience Specific skills or qualifications necessary to be successful If applicable, note any travel, evening, or weekend requirements If the role involves working with sensitive information, include: “Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters” In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $2,000–$2,500 per season. This range reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Architectural---Design-Studies_JREQ-002418": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Architectural + Design Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Visual + Performing Arts, Department of Architectural + Design Studies is currently seeking individuals to teach undergraduate and graduate Architectural Studies and Interior Architecture courses for the 2026-2027 academic calendar year. We are seeking multiple adjunct instructors for foundational architectural studies courses and major-specific courses for the following Undergraduate Architectural Studies and Interior Architecture Majors : Architectural Sketching (4-hour studio) Building Information Modeling (REVIT and RHINO) (4-hour studio) Interior Hospitality Studio (6-hour studio) Graduate Interior Architecture: Graduate Design Theory All courses are in-person unless noted otherwise. Each lecture course meets as indicated above. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $4,700-$4,800 per course. This range reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person in their assigned time blocks through the entire semester. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s  Faculty Handbook . Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Bartender---Misselwood-Events_JREQ-002383-2": {
      "title": "Bartender - Misselwood Events",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview Misselwood at Endicott College is a breathtaking oceanfront estate with historic charm, offering panoramic views and serving as the premier location for world-class events in Beverly, MA. We are seeking bartenders to work our weddings and events during the season.  This role requires work on weekends. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities ·        Responsibly serve alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages to event guest ·        Accurately check IDs ·        Responsible for monetary transactions while operating the cash register ·        Perform the set up and break down of the bar ·        Cleaning and ensuring dish machine is turned off at the end of the night ·        Responsible for counting empty beer bottles and soda bottles for event inventory sheet ·        Responsible for refilling the juice, sodas, beer and wine behind the bar for events ·        Restocking and keeping track of inventory needs ·        Other duties as assigned Reporting Structure Reports to the Director of Event Operations. During events, will take direction from head bartender Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities Core Competencies Reliability:   able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization:   organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills:   has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability:   shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through:   takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service:   anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership:   identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player:   shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills   ·        18 years or older ·        ServeSafe or TIPS certified required ·        Must be able to work late hours ·        Must be able to work weekends and holidays ·        Required to stand for long periods of time ·        Must be able to lift up to 35 pounds ·        Excellent communication and customer service skills In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay for this position is $6.75 per hour PLUS tips. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
